WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:04.759
It seems like only yesterday that The Office
— the American take on the BBC's original

00:00:04.759 --> 00:00:06.899
workplace comedy — closed its doors.

00:00:06.899 --> 00:00:11.620
And while many members of its memorable cast
have moved on to other projects or pursuits,

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:16.109
we can't help but wonder: Whatever happened
to David Denman, the actor who played Pam's

00:00:16.109 --> 00:00:18.280
ex-fiancé, Roy Anderson?

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:22.539
We know Roy struck it rich with his own gravel
company, married a restaurant owner, and even

00:00:22.539 --> 00:00:23.840
learned how to play piano …

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:33.030
[Playing piano and singing] "She's got a way
about her/I don't know what it is"

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:36.950
… but that all took place in the fantasy
land of Scranton, Pennsylvania.

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:39.320
What did Denman really do after The Office?

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:43.340
Let's take a closer look at what he's been
up to since viewers said goodbye to Dunder

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:44.460
Mifflin.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:45.899
He bossed around Steve Jobs

00:00:45.899 --> 00:00:50.190
Well, he bossed around the Ashton Kutcher
version of Steve Jobs.

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:51.570
"Listen, Steve.

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:52.940
You're good.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:55.000
You're damn good.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.750
But you're an a--hole."

00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:02.050
Denman played the small but important role
of programming pioneer and Pong creator Al

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:05.500
Alcorn in the 2013 biographical drama Jobs.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:09.390
Though it's not the most memorable part in
the critically panned film, not everyone can

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:14.080
claim that they hurled a profane insult at
the late co-founder and former CEO of Apple.

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:17.090
That's a long way from stacking boxes for
Dunder Mifflin.

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:19.360
But that wasn't Denmen's only 2013 gig.

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:24.130
He also stepped into the shoes of Private
McQuarrie in the post-apocalyptic sci-fi action

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:29.409
flick After Earth — the second movie to
star father-and-son duo Will and Jaden Smith.

00:01:29.409 --> 00:01:31.780
"Might wanna go easy on him, Sarge.

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:34.729
That's the Prime Commander's son right there."

00:01:34.729 --> 00:01:39.440
The film was widely panned by critics and
viewers alike, and it has gone down as one

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:43.400
of both Smith's and director M. Night Shyamalan's
least memorable projects.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:47.140
Fortunately for those involved, it didn't
turn out to be quite the career-demolishing

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:52.650
disaster it may have seemed — Shyamalan
rebounded with Split in 2017, while both Smiths

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:55.079
always have plenty of projects in the pipeline.

00:01:55.079 --> 00:01:56.090
As for Denman?

00:01:56.090 --> 00:01:59.660
After Earth's failure definitely didn't stop
him from landing more roles.

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:01.000
He went to boot camp

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:06.240
"You know, I do have a gun in my cubby, and
I will use it."

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:11.520
In order to prepare for his role as Boon in
the biographical war thriller 13 Hours: The

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:16.069
Secret Soldiers of Benghazi, Denman put himself
through boot camp — but not just to learn

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:17.370
how to shoot guns.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:21.790
The actor, who starred in the flick alongside
fellow Office alum John Krasinski, wanted

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:24.409
to really get into the mind of elite operatives.

00:02:24.409 --> 00:02:25.409
He told Backstage,

00:02:25.409 --> 00:02:26.739
"They're of a different ilk.

00:02:26.739 --> 00:02:31.129
They do stuff that I don't necessarily understand
and put themselves in harm's way without batting

00:02:31.129 --> 00:02:32.340
an eye."

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:36.319
Denman was also surprised to learn about the
positive impact The Office had on the actual

00:02:36.319 --> 00:02:38.079
secret soldiers of Benghazi, saying,

00:02:38.079 --> 00:02:42.610
"One of these guys came up after a screening
and said, 'We watched The Office like crazy.

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:44.010
It got us through so much.'

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:48.219
[...] I sat there in awe that some guy overseas,
trying to protect our interests, was using

00:02:48.219 --> 00:02:50.379
a silly comedy as a survival tool.

00:02:50.379 --> 00:02:52.079
My brain had an explosion.

00:02:52.079 --> 00:02:54.109
I was really moved by that."

00:02:54.109 --> 00:02:58.980
All we wanna know is: How many times did those
badass soldiers force The Office's Jim and

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:01.329
Roy to reenact their on-screen rivalry?

00:03:01.329 --> 00:03:04.739
"I'm gonna kill Jim Halpert."

00:03:04.739 --> 00:03:06.559
He put a ring on it

00:03:06.559 --> 00:03:10.449
Though Denman hasn't spent much time in the
spotlight for his various supporting roles,

00:03:10.449 --> 00:03:15.090
his marriage to Swedish-American actress and
former Fear the Walking Dead star Mercedes

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:18.639
Mason has garnered the attention of celebrity-adoring
media.

00:03:18.639 --> 00:03:23.959
The couple tied the knot in 2014, and Denman
celebrated their one-year anniversary on Instagram.

00:03:23.959 --> 00:03:29.180
It really does look like everyday is getting
better for the two — or should we say three.

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:32.900
Denman and Mason took to Instagram to announce
that they were expecting their first child.

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:37.049
And in January 2018, Mason gave birth to a
baby boy.

00:03:37.049 --> 00:03:40.909
As usual, Denman headed over to Instagram
to share the news — and compliment his wife

00:03:40.909 --> 00:03:43.280
for being such "a champ."

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:45.379
No stranger to the small screen

00:03:45.379 --> 00:03:49.099
Though Denman hasn't really been a leading
man yet, you've definitely seen him on some

00:03:49.099 --> 00:03:50.419
of your favorite shows.

00:03:50.419 --> 00:03:54.590
He's made supporting appearances on Person
of Interest, Vegas, How to Get Away with Murder,

00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:58.319
Two and a Half Men, Impress Me, Mad Men, and
True Detective.

00:03:58.319 --> 00:04:01.939
Come to think of it, he's actually been pretty
hard to miss.

00:04:01.939 --> 00:04:05.979
He's also been featured as a prominent recurring
cast member in Parenthood and Outcast.

00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:10.549
With an ever-growing resumé, expect to keep
seeing Denman pop up on your favorite series

00:04:10.549 --> 00:04:12.069
for years to come.

00:04:12.069 --> 00:04:15.569
That is, if he isn't busy landing larger roles
on the big screen.

00:04:15.569 --> 00:04:17.680
He rubs elbows with the Hollywood elite

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:23.780
In 2017, Denman appeared alongside some big-name
talent in director Steven Soderbergh's heist

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:27.169
comedy Logan Lucky, as car dealer Moody Chapman.

00:04:27.169 --> 00:04:29.250
"I love stick!

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:31.300
I'm a big fan of stick!"

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:36.380
The film boasts a cavalcade of household names
including the likes of Channing Tatum, Adam

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:38.970
Driver, Katie Holmes, and Daniel Craig.

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:43.189
Certainly not bad company for Denman — especially
considering how successful the kooky caper

00:04:43.189 --> 00:04:44.189
turned out.

00:04:44.189 --> 00:04:48.710
Logan Lucky gained critical praise for its
goofball humor and pitch-perfect ensemble

00:04:48.710 --> 00:04:52.870
cast, and it stands out as a recent highlight
on Denman's CV.

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:54.909
A bright future in film

00:04:54.909 --> 00:04:58.780
We certainly haven't seen the last of Denman,
who's come a long way since playing Roy.

00:04:58.780 --> 00:05:04.430
In 2018, the versatile actor starred alongside
Kelly Macdonald in the Marc Turtletaub-directed

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:05.620
movie Puzzle.

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:10.020
The film centers around a suburban mother
who discovers her penchant for puzzles — changing

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:12.210
both her and her family's lives.

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:17.350
It's also an adaptation of the 2010 Argentine
film Rompecabezas, which was nominated for

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:20.270
the Golden Bear at the Berlin International
Film Festival.

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:24.759
For Denman though, it's another step in the
right direction toward an increasingly impressive

00:05:24.759 --> 00:05:25.759
filmography.

00:05:25.759 --> 00:05:26.759
Thanks for watching!

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:29.389
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:29.389 --> 00:05:31.490
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

